  "description": "What: the RABBIT HUNT (CE-4649 part D, AN-21a-h; docs/designs/animals/DESIGN_Animals.md 4c; the fun pack, R-4281) - on test-town two HUNTERS (type 214, the 12-gauge, a standing rule to engage rabbits and birds, never people) walk south from (198-203,300) to (198-203,346-352) in the field east of the North Wood (the wood's east edge is x 160, y 300-380); two HUNTING DOGS range ahead of them; three RABBITS sit at the wood's edge (x 176-179, y 358-376). The dogs flush the rabbits (a dog inside a rabbit's flight distance), the rabbits freeze crouched then bolt in zigzags for the wood, the hunters shoot. Judge: (1) at least two rabbits flee (mode Flee) (2) at least three rounds are fired at rabbits (3) at least one rabbit has health 0 (4) NEVER a round at a dog or at a person. All points are inside 0-400 m. The bag per hunter is not counted here (no Points / Best parent: CE-3468). Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh rabbit-hunt"
 },
